<blockquote>
<p>with ceilings at least 15m in height.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Just say 15m. Or better yet roll that dimension in with the width and height.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>To prevent the spread of SCP-1803-1 beyond SCP-1803, cables suspending SCP-1803 should be no greater than 15mm in diameter and should be spaced no closer than 0.5m together at their anchor points.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Remove &quot;To prevent the spread of SCP-1803-1 beyond SCP-1803&quot;. The containment procedures don't need to explain the &quot;why&quot; for anything they specify. The reader should be able to deduce the &quot;why&quot; while reading the description. You want the reader to think &quot;Why the hell is that necessary?&quot; and then later think &quot;Oooohhhh&#8230;now I see.&quot; For instance, you get it right here: &quot;Absolutely no SCP decommissioning is to take place within a 10km radius of SCP-1803.&quot;</p>

